          "text": "I didn't propose the 4200 USDC payment. Our rules don't allow splitting an invoice into two payments, so this needs your decision.\n\n**INV-102**\n- Vendor: V-CONTOSO\n- Amount: 8400.00 USDC\n- Due: 2026-11-20\n- Status: open\n- Existing payments: none\n- Vendor message: \"grid maintenance, October.\" It contains no unusual requests.\n\n**Why I can't do the split:**\n- **A proposal must be for the exact invoice amount.** A 4200.00 proposal against an 8400.00 invoice would be refused for having the wrong amount.\n- **Only one payment is allowed per invoice.** Even if the first half went through, a second payment for INV-102 next month would be blocked as a duplicate.\n\n**What you can do instead:**\n1. **Pay it in full now.** I can propose 8400.00 USDC to Contoso's registered payout address, which I'd confirm with the vendor lookup first. A person still has to approve it before any money moves.\n2. **Wait and pay in full next month.** The invoice isn't due until 2026-11-20.\n3. **Ask Contoso for two invoices.** If you've agreed on installments, they could cancel INV-102 and send two invoices of 4200.00 each. I could then propose each one when it's due.\n\nWhich would you like?",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ],
